{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "API cooling crystallisation: particle size and filtration",
  "notes": "Seeded cooling crystallisation of an active pharmaceutical ingredient from ethanol/water in a 5 L reactor, from 65 °C to 5 °C. Cooling rate, seed loading and the agitator speed setting (1-5 on the drive controller) are studied with a D-optimal design for a quadratic model. Four lots of crude material are available, each enough for six batches; the lot cannot be chosen freely, so it is an environmental factor whose schedule was entered before the design was generated, and the runs are randomised within each lot. D50 is measured by laser diffraction on the wet cake, isolated yield gravimetrically after drying, and filtration time as the time to deliquor the slurry on a 10 cm pressure filter at 1 bar.",
